# Claim C4 (use-case 06): a generator over a map whose &: spread
# template contains a RELATIVE reference kills the whole model. The
# two ports: lines alone evaluate to {"a":{"containerPort":1,"port":1}};
# adding any generator over $.ports (pack or each, even with an empty
# template) makes the run exit 1 — the generator's view of the source
# still holds the unresolved .containerPort and it never fires. A
# literal spread template, or one using absolute refs, is fine.
# reference-language.md documents this composition: "A generator's
# data can still be merged into by a sibling statement, an include or
# a spread after it first looks complete" (generators wait for it).
# Not a hang: evaluation terminates in the error.
# expected: {"out":{"a":{}},"ports":{"a":{"containerPort":1,"port":1}}}
# actual:   exit 1, [aontu/mapval_no_gen] at $.out, canon shows
#           "port":.containerPort unresolved inside the pack's data
ports: { a: { containerPort: 1 } }
ports: &: { port: .containerPort }
out: pack($.ports, {})
